  m_Name: AirCompressorData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  engineName: 'Air Compressor '
  engineDescription: An Air Compressor is a mechanical device used to increase the
    pressure of atmospheric air by reducing its volume or converting mechanical energy
    into pneumatic pressure. Its main components include the compressor casing, cylinder
    or compression chamber, piston or rotating element, inlet valve, discharge valve,
    crankshaft, connecting rod, bearings, and cooling system. During operation, atmospheric
    air enters through the inlet valve and is trapped inside the compression chamber.
    The compressor mechanism reduces the volume occupied by the air, causing its
    pressure and temperature to increase. The compressed air is then discharged through
    the outlet valve and stored or supplied directly to pneumatic equipment. Air
    compressors are widely used in manufacturing plants, workshops, construction
    equipment, pneumatic tools, refrigeration systems, and industrial automation.
    From an engineering perspective, understanding compression processes, pressure
    ratio, volumetric efficiency, heat transfer, lubrication, cooling, leakage, vibration,
    and maintenance is essential for achieving efficient and reliable compressor
    performance.
  engineCategory: Engineering
